    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>For anyone stumbling over here like me - I had success with escaping the=
 semicolon and the newline:</p>

<p>First step: the semicolon. This way, we do not break the ssh command:</p=
>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">ssh &lt;host&gt; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">echo=
</span> <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">test</span>\;<span class=3D"hljs-buil=
t_in">ls</span>
                    ^ backslash!
</code></pre>

<p>Listed the remote hosts /home directory (logged in as root), whereas</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">ssh &lt;host&gt; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">echo=
</span> <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">test</span>;<span class=3D"hljs-built=
_in">ls</span>
                    ^ NO backslash
</code></pre>

<p>listed the current working directory.</p>

<p>Next step: breaking up the line:</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">                      v another backslash!
ssh &lt;host&gt; <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class=3D"h=
ljs-built_in">test</span>\;\
<span class=3D"hljs-built_in">ls</span>
</code></pre>

<p>This again listed the remote working directory - improved formatting:</p=
>

<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">ssh &lt;host&gt;\
  <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">echo</span> <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">t=
est</span>\;\
  <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">ls</span>
</code></pre>

<p>If really nicer than here document or quotes around broken lines - well,=
 not me to decide...</p>

<p>(Using bash, Ubuntu 14.04 LTS.)</p>
