    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>The easiest way to configure your system to use single ssh sessions by d=
efault with multiplexing.</p>
<p>This can be done by creating a folder for the sockets:</p>
<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash"><span class=3D"hljs-built_in">mkdir</span> ~/.ssh/c=
ontrolmasters
</code></pre>
<p>And then adding the following to your .ssh configuration:</p>
<pre class=3D"lang-bash s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">Host *
    ControlMaster auto
    ControlPath ~/.ssh/controlmasters/%r@%h:%p.socket
    ControlPersist 10m
</code></pre>
<p>Now, you do not need to modify any of your code. This allows multiple ca=
lls to ssh and scp without creating multiple sessions, which is useful when=
 there needs to be more interaction between your local and remote machines.=
</p>
<p>Thanks to @terminus's answer, <a href=3D"http://www.cyberciti.biz/faq/li=
nux-unix-osx-bsd-ssh-multiplexing-to-speed-up-ssh-connections/" rel=3D"nofo=
llow noreferrer">http://www.cyberciti.biz/faq/linux-unix-osx-bsd-ssh-multip=
lexing-to-speed-up-ssh-connections/</a> and <a href=3D"https://en.wikibooks=
.org/wiki/OpenSSH/Cookbook/Multiplexing" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer">https:=
//en.wikibooks.org/wiki/OpenSSH/Cookbook/Multiplexing</a>.</p>
    </div>
